fcb-5d8b-9b9f-266e88925e56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571387 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrices $B$ and $C$ are upper triangular matrices since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrix $A$ is *not* an upper triangular matrix since it has a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{43} & =1\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126346" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40b938cb-f23c-5d0f-a251-58ee4d72d0a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571390 #edb/ref 1074 "The matrix $A$ is an upper triangular matrix since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nThe matrices $B$ and $C$ are *not* upper triangular matrices since they each have a non-zero element below the main diagonal: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{21} & =2\\ne 0 \\\\ {c}_{32} & =-2\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1069 "q-13785" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1071 "How can we best describe the following matrix? \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5b8d0549-8a06-5a32-8cc6-861cdf3fc65b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571401 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries below the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 10 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is an upper triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not a lower triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element above the diagonal: ${a}_{12}=10\\ne 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571336 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $D$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $D$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${D}^{T}$ is upper triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5fc95051-8b70-5447-aece-290d3854c40e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571405 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $D$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $D$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${D}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{D}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1069 "q-126474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $B$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${B}^{T}+B$ is upper triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "814b1f0e-0432-56a4-8a3b-10efb7462756" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571420 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of ${B}^{T}+B$ has all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}+B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186571315 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42114" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $A$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${A}^{T}$ is lower triangular" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e901e3e2-6ad0-5a4e-b4c9-fb5111610c41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186571448 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since ${A}^{T}$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
